# Upstream repos cloned for reference only - 1.1 GB, and each has its own .git.
# Recreate with:
#   git clone https://github.com/sonocotta/esp32-audio-dock       reference/esp32-audio-dock
#   git clone https://github.com/sonocotta/esp32-tas5805m-dac     reference/esp32-tas5805m-dac
#   git clone https://github.com/mrtoy-me/esphome-tas58xx         reference/esphome-tas58xx
reference/

# Your own installation: device YAMLs, register-dump logs, session notes.
#
# This repo ships a generic component plus example configs. Anything specific to
# YOUR devices - real names, friendly names, room labels, speaker models, PSU
# voltages, bench logs - belongs here and never gets committed. Copy an example
# out of esphome/, rename it, and work on it in local/.
#
# Deliberately a whole directory rather than per-file entries: a new device file
# is then ignored the moment you create it, instead of the next time someone
# remembers to add a rule.
local/

# Real credentials. Commit secrets.yaml.example instead.
secrets.yaml

# ESPHome / PlatformIO build output
.esphome/
build/
*.bin
*.elf

# Host-side C++ check artifacts
tools/cpp_check/*.exe
tools/cpp_check/*.obj
tools/cpp_check/*.o
tools/cpp_check/out/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor / agent local state
.claude/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Generated test signals - regenerate with tools/make_drc_staircase.py
*.wav
